[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/163374992","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/263#issuecomment-163374992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/263","id":163374992,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE2MzM3NDk5Mg==","user":{"login":"dschafer","id":2760005,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NjAwMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2760005?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer","html_url":"https://github.com/dschafer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dschafer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-12-09T20:05:39Z","updated_at":"2015-12-09T20:05:39Z","body":"We want the validator stage to be able to run independently of the values of variables; this allows us (for example) to validate and persist the query text, then send up an identifier for that persisted query along with the variable values and skip validation (because it was already validated).\n\n> This is an issue when using Relay because it can produce queries like this in some cases.\n\nSounds like this is a bug in Relay to me? @josephsavona @yungsters ?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/163374992/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/178351174","html_url":"https://github.com/graphql/graphql-js/issues/263#issuecomment-178351174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/263","id":178351174,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3ODM1MTE3NA==","user":{"login":"leebyron","id":50130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron","html_url":"https://github.com/leebyron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leebyron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-02-02T03:46:29Z","updated_at":"2016-02-02T03:46:29Z","body":"As @dschafer pointed out, we want to ensure validation is done without the variable values. This lets us ensure a query is valid statically before runtime. For example, to run validation on queries within a codebase to ensure they are valid before they are even run.\n\nI opened an issue on Relay since it certainly seems like Relay should not produce invalid queries like this.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/graphql/graphql-js/issues/comments/178351174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,